cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "closure_drift: does your version label name exactly one version of your code?"
abstract: >-
  A read-only, zero-dependency tool that measures, over any git repository,
  whether a declared version label identifies exactly one state of the
  producing code at the points where that repository publishes. Distinguishes
  release-based publication (tags) from continuous publication (commits),
  because measuring at every commit reports drift in every repository and
  therefore carries no information. Each report stamps the commit measured and
  the hash of the tool that measured it. 0.4.0 keeps the measurement script
  byte-identical to 0.3.0 and adds a negative fixture (a label-only corpus
  under one label must be flagged), the documented limitation that the tool
  checks address well-formedness and never attests re-execution, and further
  reference results.
type: software
authors:
